{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the probability that Alice wins the game, we need to analyze the sequence of events and the probabilities of each event occurring. Let's denote the probability that Alice wins the game by \\( P \\).\n\n1. **Alice's First Turn:**\n   - Alice wins immediately if she gets heads. The probability of this happening is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n   - If Alice gets tails (which happens with probability \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)), it becomes Bob's turn.\n\n2. **Bob's Turn:**\n   - If it's Bob's turn and he gets tails, he wins. The probability of this happening is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n   - If Bob gets heads (which happens with probability \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)), it returns to Alice's turn.\n\nThus, the probability that Alice wins the game can be expressed as the sum of the probabilities of the two scenarios where she wins:\n- Alice wins on her first turn.\n- Alice wins after Bob does not win on his turn and the game returns to Alice.\n\n","prefix_end":918,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,18927,429,29405,14816,279,1809,11,582,1184,311,23643,279,8500,315,4357,323,279,48216,315,1817,1538,30865,13,6771,594,78064,279,18927,429,29405,14816,279,1809,553,17767,393,1124,3593,16,13,3070,61686,594,5512,11999,25,1019,256,481,29405,14816,7069,421,1340,5221,14629,13,576,18927,315,419,12482,374,17767,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,4292,256,481,1416,29405,5221,63514,320,8206,8573,448,18927,17767,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,5731,432,9044,14261,594,2484,382,17,13,3070,32388,594,11999,25,1019,256,481,1416,432,594,14261,594,2484,323,566,5221,63514,11,566,14816,13,576,18927,315,419,12482,374,17767,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,4292,256,481,1416,14261,5221,14629,320,8206,8573,448,18927,17767,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,5731,432,4675,311,29405,594,2484,382,44500,11,279,18927,429,29405,14816,279,1809,646,3